def fibonacci(n):
    if n <= 0:
        return None
    fib_sequence = [0, 1]

    for i in range(2, n+1):
        fib_sequence.append(fib_sequence[i-1] + fib_sequence[i-2])

    return fib_sequence[-1]
```
This version of the function has a linear time complexity and is more suitable for calculating Fibonacci numbers with larger values of `n`.

